  "final": "`DocumentService.archive` in `src/service.ts` now enforces the authorization rules. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes, including the new checks.\n\n- **Visibility:** a missing, deleted or foreign-tenant document throws `Error('not found')`, whatever the actor's role.\n- **Permission:** this is checked on every visible document, including one that is already archived.\n  - An admin may archive any visible document.\n  - An editor may archive only a document they own.\n  - A viewer never may.\n  - Any other role value is also denied, so an unexpected role can't archive anything.\n  - A visible request that isn't allowed throws `Error('forbidden')`.\n- **Archiving:** an already-archived visible document returns without doing anything once permission is confirmed. Otherwise the existing repository call sets `archived` to true and appends `{actor: actor.user, document: id}` to the audit.\n- **Failures:** every check runs before any change, so a failed call leaves documents and audit untouched.\n\nI appended checks to `checks/public.cjs`. They cover each role and the three kinds of invisible document. They also cover forbidden calls, including forbidden repeats on an archived document, and a successful archive by an admin and by an editor. Each failure case asserts that documents and audit are unchanged.\n\nThe public interfaces are unchanged.",
